# ====================================================================
# SAVR Mobile App Environment Variables Configuration
# ====================================================================
# This file contains environment variables needed for the Expo mobile app.
# For GitHub Actions secrets setup, see: ../GITHUB_SECRETS_SETUP.md
#
# INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file to .env (same directory as this file)
# 2. Replace placeholder values with your actual credentials
# 3. Never commit .env to version control (it's in .gitignore)
# ====================================================================

# ====================================================================
# FIREBASE CONFIGURATION (Required - Public)
# ====================================================================
# Get these from Firebase Console > Project Settings > Your apps
# IMPORTANT: These are the SAME values as NEXT_PUBLIC_* in web app,
# but use EXPO_PUBLIC_* prefix for Expo/React Native
# Source: https://console.firebase.google.com/
#
# These values are safe to expose in client-side code (Firebase API key
# is designed to be public and is protected by Firebase security rules)

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project-id.firebaseapp.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project-id.appspot.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your-messaging-sender-id
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your-app-id

# ====================================================================
# GOOGLE OAUTH CONFIGURATION (Required - Public)
# ====================================================================
# Get from: https://console.cloud.google.com/ > APIs & Services > Credentials
# You need THREE separate OAuth 2.0 Client IDs:
#
# 1. WEB CLIENT ID:
#    - Application type: Web application
#    - Used for: Firebase Google Sign-In on web and mobile
#
# 2. IOS CLIENT ID:
#    - Application type: iOS
#    - Bundle ID: Must match your iOS app bundle ID (com.savr.app)
#
# 3. ANDROID CLIENT ID:
#    - Application type: Android
#    - Package name: Must match your Android package (com.savr.app)
#    - SHA-1 fingerprint: Required (get from EAS or local keystore)
#
# IMPORTANT: The Web Client ID is REQUIRED even for mobile apps when
# using Firebase Authentication with Google Sign-In
# Source: https://firebase.google.com/docs/auth/ios/google-signin

EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=your-ios-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=your-android-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ====================================================================
# VARIABLE SUMMARY
# ====================================================================
# Total: 9 variables
# - Firebase Config: 6 (public)
# - Google OAuth: 3 (public - Client IDs are safe to expose)
#
# All variables are public and safe to include in mobile app builds.
# They are protected by:
# - Firebase security rules (for Firebase services)
# - OAuth redirect URI restrictions (for Google Sign-In)
# - SHA-1 certificate fingerprint validation (for Android)
# ====================================================================

# ====================================================================
# ADDITIONAL NOTES
# ====================================================================
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* vs NEXT_PUBLIC_*:
# - Web app (Next.js) uses NEXT_PUBLIC_* prefix
# - Mobile app (Expo) uses EXPO_PUBLIC_* prefix
# - Both access the same Firebase backend
# - During CI/CD, GitHub secrets use NEXT_PUBLIC_* names and are
#   mapped to EXPO_PUBLIC_* for mobile builds
#
# For EAS Build:
# - These variables are embedded in the app during build
# - Configure them in eas.json or pass via GitHub Actions
# - See: https://docs.expo.dev/build-reference/variables/
#
# For Local Development:
# - Create mobile/.env with these values
# - Run: npm start or eas build --profile development
# ====================================================================
